Waverley Council is committed to the highest standards of environmental performance
and stewardship of our local area. Council has established long-term environmental
targets for Council and Community, covering greenhouse emissions, transport, climate
resilience, urban ecology, water management and the sustainable management of waste
and materials. Our targets are informed by the best available science and support
Ecologically Sustainable Development (ESD) through the following objectives:
• Reducing greenhouse gas emissions to net zero;
• Increasing the use of renewable energy sources;
• Conserving water resources;
• Reducing reliance on mains water supply through the collection and treatment
of rainwater and greywater;
• Adapting and responding to climate change to reduce community vulnerability
to local climate change impacts and managing climate risks;
• Reducing waste during construction and the ongoing use of the building;
• Increasing recycling of waste and use of recycled products;
• Reducing the environmental impact from building materials through the
reduction, re-use and recycling of materials, resources and building
components;
• Protecting and improving local biodiversity of sites and surrounding areas.

